            <ArticleTitle>Incidence of rapid resolution of defects on stress thallium scans.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>458-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A prospective study was performed to determine the frequency with which defects on stress thallium images undergo rapid resolution. Analysis of paired views showed that 15% of the defects present in anterior views resolve in less than 30 minutes. This study documents the loss of sensitivity that can occur if imaging does not begin promptly after injection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
